docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:1:# PRD: Stage Commit Classification and Commit Tag Guidance
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:5:Personal Symphony can create a **Stage Commit** after a **Stage Agent** completes, but the current
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:6:classification model is too shallow. Each stage has one configured commit type, and the generated
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:7:message cannot reflect issue labels, richer repository taxonomy, or commit guidance that a
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:10:Operators need **Stage Commit** messages that communicate what kind of work happened without asking
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:11:agents to create commits manually. The system also needs a clear answer to whether richer tagging
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:13:**Stage Commit** behavior with agent-side Git workflows.
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:19:1. **Runtime Settings**-driven **Stage Commit Classification**: the authoritative source for commit
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:20:   type or tag used when Symphony renders a **Stage Commit** message.
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:21:2. Repository-owned commit tag guidance in `tags.json`: the vocabulary that explains valid
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:22:   four-character commit tags to agents and commit rendering.
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:24:**Runtime Settings** remain authoritative for commit metadata. A personalized commit skill may guide
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:26:the **Stage Commit** and must not override resolved **Stage Commit Classification** unless
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:31:1. As an operator, I want **Stage Commits** to use issue labels when selecting a commit type, so that
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:33:2. As an operator, I want each **Stage Agent** to keep its own default **Stage Commit
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:35:3. As an operator, I want **Runtime Settings** to define the repository's commit classification
docs/prd/0024-stage-commit-classification-and-commit-skill.md:36:   taxonomy, so that commit messages do not depend on each agent's memory.
