+254:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may use its planner stage as a PRD review gate for already-refined issues.
+255:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should use **Stage Commit** to create local engineer-stage commits before review.
+256:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should keep **Stage Push** disabled unless remote branch publication is deliberately enabled.
+257:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should use reviewer-stage comments and a **Human Attention Status** for review findings that require operator triage.
+258:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should have the reviewer stage run focused verification when practical before moving work to `Done`.
+259:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may increase concurrency when its **Loop-Start Branch** is not a **Protected Trunk Branch** because **Task Branch Integration** can integrate unrelated concurrently completed **Task Branches**.
+260:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should use a dedicated non-trunk **Loop-Start Branch** so completed **Task Branches** do not auto-merge into the Product Repository trunk.
+261:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may open a **Batch Pull Request** from its dedicated **Loop-Start Branch** to its **Protected Trunk Branch** after **Orchestration Idle**.
+262:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should remove merged **Agent Worktrees** and delete merged **Task Branches** to avoid local branch buildup.
+263:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should prevent accidental dogfood dispatch from the Product Repository trunk.
+264:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should define a **Protected Path Policy** for release and package files once that policy exists.
+265:- An **Idempotent Bootstrap** must preserve existing Runtime Contract and Local Environment files.
+266:- A **Workspace Repository** contains at most one **Runtime Home**.
+267:- Personal Symphony commands must be run from the root of a **Workspace Repository**.
+268:- Personal Symphony exits before Bootstrap when the current directory is not the root of a **Workspace Repository**.
+269:- A **Runtime Home** contains the **Runtime Contract**, user-editable settings, and internal state.
+270:- The **Runtime Contract** contains **Runtime Settings**.
+271:- The **Runtime Contract** contains an **Agent Prompt**.
+276:- The **Runtime Settings** contain a **Git Policy**.
+278:- A **Workspace Repository** may define a **Protected Path Policy**.
+283:- Each **Agent Worktree** checks out one **Task Branch**.
+284:- Each **Task Branch** starts from the **Loop-Start Branch**.
+285:- Each **Task Branch** name starts with the **Task Branch Prefix** and includes the task's stable issue number.
+286:- If a task enters work without an existing **Task Branch**, the **Task Branch** starts from the current **Loop-Start Branch**.
+287:- If a task already has a **Task Branch**, Symphony reuses it.
+291:- Symphony may auto-merge a completed **Task Branch** into the **Loop-Start Branch** only when the **Loop-Start Branch** is not a **Protected Trunk Branch**.
+292:- Auto-merge of a **Task Branch** into the **Loop-Start Branch** keeps the final **Loop-Start Branch** update fast-forward only.
+293:- If the **Loop-Start Branch** cannot fast-forward directly to a completed **Task Branch**, Symphony may update the **Task Branch** by merging the current **Loop-Start Branch** into it from the **Agent Worktree**, then fast-forward the **Loop-Start Branch** to the updated **Task Branch**.
+295:- Auto-merge, **Startup Reconciliation**, and **Manual Task Merge** are **Task Branch Integration** paths.
+300:- **Manual Task Merge** accepts issue identifiers such as `20` and `#20`; it does not accept raw **Task Branch** names.
+306:- **Startup Reconciliation** uses the same safe **Task Branch Integration** path as normal completion.
+307:- **Startup Reconciliation** does not create a **Stage Commit**, reconcile retained **Task Branches** without **Agent Worktrees**, or change tracker status after successful or already-contained reconciliation.
+309:- **Runtime State** records **Task Branch Integration** diagnostics for direct fast-forwards, update-then-fast-forward integrations, already-contained branches, and integration attention.
+310:- A **Merge Attention Status** is a **Human Attention Status**.
+312:- A **Human Attention Status** is paused and not dispatchable.
+313:- The default **Task Cleanup Policy** removes an **Agent Worktree** after its **Task Branch** is merged.
+314:- The default **Task Cleanup Policy** keeps a merged **Task Branch**.
+315:- A **Stage Commit** may be created when a configured stage completes with code changes.
+316:- A **Stage Commit** may use a **Stage Commit Classification** when rendering its commit message.
+317:- **Stage Commit Classification** uses matching issue labels before the stage default.
+318:- When matching issue labels resolve to conflicting classifications for a commit-enabled stage, Symphony pauses the task in a **Human Attention Status** before creating a **Stage Commit**.
+319:- A **Workspace Repository** may define **Stage Commit Tag Guidance** in `tags.json`.
+320:- **Stage Commit Tag Guidance** is a JSON array of objects with `tag` and `instructions` fields.
+321:- A **Stage Commit Tag Guidance** `tag` is a four-character commit tag or type value used by **Stage Commit Classification**.
+322:- **Stage Commit Tag Guidance** should be included in every **Stage Commit** step.
+323:- A **Stage Push** happens only after a **Stage Commit** is successfully created.
+324:- A **Stage Push** happens before the stage moves to its success project state.
+325:- Runtime Settings enable a **Stage Push** with `commit.push` on a configured stage.
+326:- A missing `commit.push` setting means the **Stage Push** is disabled.
+327:- Bootstrapped Runtime Settings include `commit.push` as `false` in each example stage commit policy.
+328:- A **Stage Push** sends the **Stage Commit** to the currently checked-out **Task Branch**.
+329:- A **Stage Push** pushes the current **Task Branch** tip, including earlier unpushed commits on that branch.
+330:- A **Stage Push** is a non-force push.
+331:- A **Stage Push** uses the current **Task Branch** upstream when one exists.
+332:- A **Stage Push** creates an upstream on `origin` when the current **Task Branch** has no upstream.
+333:- A **Stage Push** happens before any auto-merge attempt.
+334:- **Task Branch Integration** must not force-push a **Task Branch** after **Stage Push**.
+336:- A failed **Stage Push** prevents the stage from moving to its success project state.
+337:- A failed **Stage Push** is retryable.
+340:- Runtime Settings configure **Stage Goal Handoff** with `goal.enabled` on a stage.
+343:- Bootstrapped Runtime Settings include `goal.enabled` as `false` in each example stage.
+368:- An **Ordered Queue** is named with issue identifiers from the Workspace Repository issue tracker.
+377:- An **Ordered Queue Entry** is invalid when it is malformed, missing from the Workspace Repository issue tracker, absent from the configured GitHub Project, terminal, or not dispatchable.
+402:- A **Pull Request Base Branch** must be configured explicitly in Runtime Settings.
+403:- The **Runtime Settings** may contain a **Pull Request Policy**.
+414:- The **Runtime Contract** is version-controlled with the Workspace Repository.
+435:- **Audio Notification Configuration** does not change **Runtime Settings**.
+466:- `symphony update` updates the installed **CLI Package** and does not require a **Workspace Repository**.
